            [M-1] Type mismatch when passing cloid to
            cancelOrderByCloid

             SEVERITY: Medium                                    IMPACT: Medium


             STATUS: Resolved                                    LIKELIHOOD: Medium




            Target
             • LqTrader.sol


            Description:
            The function closeOrdersByCloid accepts cloids as uint64, but passes each value directly
            to cancelOrderByCloid.

              function closeOrdersByCloid(uint32[] calldata assets, uint64[]
                  calldata cloids) external override onlyCloser {
                  require(assets.length /= cloids.length, "Length Mismatch!");
                   for (uint256 i = 0; i < assets.length; i++) {
              />       CoreWriterLib.cancelOrderByCloid(assets[i], cloids[i]);
                   }
              }


            However, the target function requires the uint128:

              />   function cancelOrderByCloid(uint32 asset, uint128 cloid) internal {
                       coreWriter.sendRawAction(
                           abi.encodePacked(uint8(1),
                   HLConstants.CANCEL_ORDER_BY_CLOID_ACTION, abi.encode(asset, cloid))
                       );
                   }


            In HyperCore, the cloid is uint128. Therefore, using uint64[] in LqTrader silently
            truncates the domain of valid cloid from 128 bits → 64 bits. As a result, any cloid values

FLEX LABS   SMART CONTRACT SECURITY ASSESSMENT                                    VERSION 1.1




            above 2^64-1 could never be passed through this function.


