Instance Storage Nonce Exhaustion
ID                           Severity              Status                     Found in
OS-MLS-ADV-00                   High               ✓ Resolved                 d21f055

Description
User-authorized wallet actions track replay protection with a nonce high-water mark keyed by the
wallet user public key and wallet hash. In Wallet::verify_signature_nonce_is_free, the nonce
record is read from and created in contract instance storage, so every distinct signed wallet/user
pair that reaches this path can add or update state in the same bounded instance storage area.


      contracts/sollpay/src/wallet.rs

  1    fn verify_signature_nonce_is_free(
  2          env: &Env,
  3          user: BytesN<32>,
  4          wallet_hash: BytesN<32>,
  5          nonce: u64,
  6    ) {
  7          let storage_type = StorageType::Instance;
  8          let key = DataKey::SignatureNonce(user, wallet_hash);
  9          let stored_nonce: Option<StoredValue<u64>> = StoredValue::get(env, storage_type,
             key.clone());

 11          if let Some(mut stored_nonce) = stored_nonce {
 12              if nonce <= *stored_nonce {
 13                  panic_with_error!(env, SollpayErrors::SignatureNonceUsed);
 14              }
 15              if nonce - *stored_nonce > MAX_NONCE_ADVANCE {
 16                  panic_with_error!(env, SollpayErrors::SignatureNonceTooHigh);
 17              }
 18              *stored_nonce = nonce;
 19          } else {
 20              if nonce > MAX_NONCE_ADVANCE {
 21                  panic_with_error!(env, SollpayErrors::SignatureNonceTooHigh);
 22              }
 23              _ = StoredValue::create(env, storage_type, key, nonce);
 24          }
 25    }

Nonce high-water mark stored in instance storage


The signed forwarding and vault-update paths call this nonce check after verifying the wallet
user’s ed25519 signature, and the documentation describes the nonce as one stored high-
water value per (user public key, wallet hash) pair. Because these nonce entries are kept in
instance storage rather than a storage area whose growth is bounded or isolated per wallet,
normal user growth can eventually exhaust the contract’s instance storage.


© 2026 Otter Audits LLC. All Rights Reserved.                                                   6 / 28
                                                              Mercury Labs Sollpay Security Assessment



An attacker can accelerate the exhaustion by creating multiple wallets and using them to con-
sume nonce entries, which will result in a denial of service scenario once no further user requests
can be processed.

Remediation
Move signature nonce tracking out of the shared bounded instance storage layout. Store the
high-water nonce in a storage location whose growth is bounded by the wallet model.

Patch
Resolved in 6b6c007.




