Issue M-2: NavOracleAutomation.performUpkeep() can
revert wasting funds
Source: https://github.com/sherlock-audit/2026-02-mezzanine-feb-25th/issues/26


Summary
Chainlink Automation calls checkUpkeep() offchain and executes performUpkeep() when
it returns true. However it doesn't check some cases which cause revert. As a result,
Chainlink will submit reverting transactions which consume funds.


Vulnerability Detail
checkUpkeep() returns true as soon as vetoPeriod has passed.

      function checkUpkeep(
          bytes calldata checkData
      ) external view returns (bool upkeepNeeded, bytes memory performData) {
          checkData;
          if (!hasPendingNav()) return (false, "");
 @>       if (block.timestamp < pendingReadyAt) return (false, "");
          return (true, "");
      }

      function hasPendingNav() public view returns (bool) {
          return pendingReadyAt != 0;
      }

      function performUpkeep(bytes calldata performData) external {
          performData;
          if (!hasPendingNav()) revert NoPendingNav();
          uint256 readyAt = pendingReadyAt;
          if (block.timestamp < readyAt) revert NotReady(readyAt);
          _applyPending();
      }

      function _applyPending() internal {
          bool isYield = pendingIsYield;
          uint256 deltaUSDC = pendingDeltaUSDC;
          uint256 readyAt = pendingReadyAt;

         _clearPending();

         if (isYield) {
             IVault(vault).distributeYield(deltaUSDC);
         } else {

               ILossManager(lossManager).applyLoss(deltaUSDC);
          }
      }

However there are other conditions when IssuanceVault.distributeYield() and LossMan
ager.applyLoss() can revert:
   1) Both execute IssuanceVault._advanceEpochAndValidate() which ensures enough
      time has passed in current epoch. So it will revert if epochDuration > vetoPeriod.

      function _advanceEpochAndValidate() internal returns (uint256 newEpochId) {
          uint64 ts = uint64(block.timestamp);
 @>       if (ts < epochStart + epochDuration) revert EpochTooSoon();
          ...
      }

  2) It reverts if loss amount is too big:

      function applyLoss(
          uint256 usdcLoss
      ) external onlyNavOracle whenNotPaused(PauseCategory.PROTOCOL) {
          if (usdcLoss == 0) revert ZeroAmount();
 @>       if (maxLossPerTxUSDC != 0 && usdcLoss > maxLossPerTxUSDC) revert
 ,→   LimitExceeded();

  3) Reverts when there are no tranches:

 function distributeYield(
     uint256 usdcReported
 ) external nonReentrant onlyNavOracle whenNotPaused(PauseCategory.PROTOCOL) {
     if (tranches.length == 0) revert NoTranchesAdded();



Impact
Chainlink Automation can execute reverting transactions which consumes protocol
funds. Mainly when epochDuration > vetoPeriod. It is reasonable to assume because MAX
_EPOCH_DURATION_LIMIT = 30 days, while MAX_VETO_PERIOD = 5 days.
However it's not clear what is Chainlink's behaviour when performUpkeep() reverts
multiple times in a row.


