Issue M-1: Partial deleverage locks collateral in Mor-
pho and allows to avoid fee [RESOLVED]
Source: https://github.com/sherlock-audit/2026-04-spiral-stake-apr-27th/issues/13


Summary
Deleverage is supposed to close position: withdraw all collateral and repay all debt. But
user has option to withdraw collateral partially, in this case user doesn't have option to
withdraw remaining collateral. Such partial deleverage also allows to avoid paying fee.


Vulnerability Detail
Flow is following:
   1) Flashloan is taken for position's loan amount
  2) Full loan is repayed
  3) Collateral is withdrawn
  4) Position is closed
However user has ability to specify how much collateral to withdraw:

