Suppose following example:
   1) User creates 2x leveraged position with loan = 1000, collateral = 2000
  2) Then calls deleverage() with amount 1500
  3) It will repay 1000 loan and withdraw 1500 collateral
  4) Then convert collateral to loan and repay flashloan
  5) So in the end transfers 500 loan token to user
  6) Remaining 500 collateral is still in Morpho
  7) Collateral can't be withdrawn because position is closed: position.open = false.
     The only option is to contact admin and withdraw it via manual mode.
Moreover such vector allows to avoid paying fee. Let's consider following scenario:
   1) Same position as above: loan = 1000, collateral = 2000
  2) Yield fee is 10%, assume yield is 10%, so collateral grows to 2200
  3) It means that yield fee should be 200 * 10% = 20
  4) But user can call deleverage() with amount 1000
  5) It will calculate that user lost any surplus collateral over loan, because totalAmount
     Returned = 0 and hence won't take fee:
