Discussion
Bhimgouda

 Valid Medium, as user gets to choose the amount, so stuck collateral is a real path only
when user explicitly chooses to withdraw less than full collateral. Even passing 0
withdraws everything correctly.
The fee bypass is self-punishing without admin cooperation, as user loses the stuck
collateral to avoid paying the yield fee.
Context on the parameter: we previously fetched collateral directly from Morpho
(morphoPosition.collateral), but that created a front-running DoS where an attacker
could supply 1 wei of collateral to the proxy, causing the pre-built swap calldata to
mismatch and revert (as partial deleverage is forbidden as it helps with bypassing fees)
The amountCollateral parameter was the fix for that. Open to a better approach that
prevents both the DoS and partial deleverage.
